  "interpretation": [
    "Targeted lower-zone placement transfers strongly but not absolutely: it is componentwise supported on five of six prospective materials at dimension four and all six at dimension eight.",
    "B05 is a real counterexample to a universal four-layer placement rule: U4 has markedly smaller bottom-flux and cumulative-exchange error than L4, although L4 has slightly smaller mapped-profile RMSE. By the frozen vector L4 is therefore not componentwise supported on B05.",
    "The L4-L6-R8 targeted ladder is fully componentwise monotone on four of six materials. B02 and B16 exhibit an output tradeoff in which greater dimension improves bottom-flux and profile fidelity but slightly worsens cumulative exchange/storage.",
    "Several materials reach an R16-operator exchange-error floor by L6 or R8, while mapped-profile error continues to decrease with dimension. This reinforces purpose-dependent dimension selection.",
    "B05 remains structurally difficult even at R8: R8 improves strongly over L4/L6 and U8 but remains above the R16-operator floor, so its residual should be decomposed with same-partition CoRichards before any closure retuning."
  ],
